# Line endings and binary handling.
#
# Without this git guessed per file: the PDFs showed as modified
# forever, and every source file carried line-ending churn that buried
# the real diffs.
#
# Text is normalised to LF in the repository and checked out in the
# platform's own form.  The BASIC test programs are listings typed at a
# CoCo, so they live here as ordinary text; the CR-terminated form the
# machine wants is produced when a disk image is built, not stored.

* text=auto

*.asm       text
*.inc       text
*.bas       text
*.md        text
*.py        text
*.txt       text
Makefile    text
LICENSE     text

# Real binaries.
*.rom       binary
*.bin       binary
*.dsk       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.zip       binary
*.pdf       binary

# Everything the PLD toolchain wrote or reads, left byte for byte.
#
# These must not be normalised, and one of them would break if it were:
# a JEDEC file carries a transmission checksum summed over its own
# bytes, so dropping a CR from every line invalidates it and a device
# programmer can refuse the part.  COCOBUB.pdf is not a PDF at all - it
# is a CUPL PDIF schematic, ASCII with CRLF - which is why the rule is
# by directory and comes after the *.pdf rule above.
#
# -text rather than binary: no conversion, but still diffable, since
# most of these are readable text.
pld/**      -text
pld/*.pdf   -text diff merge
